  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A metal surface of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;area has to be coated with nickel layer of thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> A current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> was passed through a solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8216;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo></math> seconds to coat the desired layer. The value&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is _________. (Nearest integer)</p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;Ni</mi></math>&nbsp;(density of Nickel) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mL</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>Molar mass of Nickel is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>One equivalent of substance deposited for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>96500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>(one Faraday).</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math>&nbsp;Columbus of charge can be utilised to get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of substance.</p><p>Millimoles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi></math>&nbsp;coated</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>96500</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mn>965</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>965</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>600</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>600</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mn>965</mn></mfrac><mi>mg</mi></math></p><p>Volume<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mn>965</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1608</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>161</mn></math></p>"
  }
